course: dictionary
lesson: 6410
title: Music: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Music is a word with more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to find the right one. «Listen to music» is about sounds you hear. «Sheet music» is about the written notes. A «music lesson» at school is about learning to sing, play and listen.
explain: Context can also show you a feeling. «The same pictures with different music can feel scary, sad or funny.» The pictures stay the same, but the sounds change how we feel about them.
explain: Music also appears in phrases that do not mean sounds at all. «Music to my ears» means good news, and «face the music» means accepting a punishment. The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning is right.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If «music to my ears» means good news, then «Your idea is music to my ears» should still make sense. It does, so you have understood it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Music means sounds arranged in a pleasant or interesting way, made by singing or playing instruments.
fact: «Sheet music» means the written notes that show how to play a piece.
fact: In science, music is sound made by vibrations; faster vibrations give higher notes.
fact: «Music to my ears» means good news. «Face the music» means accepting a punishment.
exercise: «The same pictures with different music can feel scary, sad or funny.» In this sentence, what does music mean? | A kind of dance | A school where you learn maths | The written notes on a page | *Sounds made by singing or playing
exercise: What is sheet music? | A loud noise from the street | A drawing of a music teacher | A cloth for wiping a piano | *The written notes that show how to play a piece
exercise: In science, what do faster vibrations give in music? | Silence | Lower notes | *Higher notes | Louder thumps
test: Ruby says, «Your idea is music to my ears!» What does she mean? | *She is pleased and likes the idea | She cannot hear the idea | She is annoyed by the noise | She wants to dance to it
test: «The Grammy Awards are voted on by members of the Recording Academy, people who work in music, not by fans.» Who votes for the Grammy Awards? | Children | Fans | *People who work in music | Scientists
exam: «Jayden broke the vase and now he must face the music.» What does face the music mean here? | Listen to the radio | *Accept the punishment | Dance to a loud song | Play the piano badly
